local.eaptls12fix (1.6.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Diagnostics for dropped connections. The watchdog log now records every
    change of association, network, access point (roams) and address with
    signal strength and channel, plus a signal heartbeat every 10 minutes.
  * On a disassociation, lost address, failed check, or before any recovery
    action, the surrounding Wi-Fi/EAP/DHCP system log (driver joins and
    disassociations, wifid, eapolclient, configd) is saved to
    /var/mobile/Media/wifi-diag/ (newest 30 kept) by the new helper
    /usr/libexec/wifi-watchdog-diag, so the reason survives log rotation.

 -- J_W_I_ <64947174+JWIMaster@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:35:00 +1100

local.eaptls12fix (1.6.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the Wi-Fi recovery watchdog undoing itself. launchd is now the only
    thing that runs it (KeepAlive); 1.5.0 also started it from postinst and
    from inside wifid/eapolclient, which raced into duplicate watchdogs that
    each restarted wifid. It exits on SIGTERM (1.5.0 trapped TERM without
    exiting, so every upgrade left the old copy running), and the package
    reaps leftover copies with a new helper, /usr/libexec/wifi-watchdog-reap.
  * Detect the real failure states from SystemConfiguration: associated with
    no address or a self-assigned 169.254.x address (renew DHCP, then restart
    wifid), associated with no traffic (restart wifid), and long periods
    powered-on but unassociated (occasional auto-join nudge). 1.5.0 treated
    "No route to host" as reachable and ignored a missing address, so the
    common ANU-Secure DHCP failure was never recovered.
  * wifid is restarted with launchctl stop (clean EAP teardown) instead of
    SIGKILL. The log rotates at 256 KB.
  * The tweak loads into eapolclient only and no longer forks processes;
    the TLS 1.2 ceiling hook is unchanged.
  * Source for the whole package (watchdog, launchd job, scripts, build.sh,
    device scenario tests) now lives in sources/EAPTLS12Fix.

 -- J_W_I_ <64947174+JWIMaster@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 06:30:00 +1100

local.eaptls12fix (1.0.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Add EAP TLS 1.2 Fix, enabling TLS 1.2 for the legacy iOS 5/6
    eapolclient so WPA2-Enterprise networks such as ANU-Secure can
    authenticate. Certificate validation is unchanged.
  * Tested on iPod3,1 iOS 5.1.1 and iPod4,1 iOS 6.1.6.

